      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=2 x^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(x)v(x))' &=u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ &=(2 x^{2})'\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(2 x^{2})\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ &=(4 x)(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(2 x^{2})(- \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &=4 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} \\\\ &\\quad +(- 2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
